ovider":"PubTator (NCBI)"},{"prefix":"2 allele rs2476601 (","exact":"R620W","postfix":") with GCA. SUMMARY:","tags":[{"name":"R620W","uri":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/snp/?term=R620W"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/MED/25405820#pubtator-9bc1a811ced8c19aea89fb3a0a3b5af3","type":"Gene Mutations","section":"Abstract (http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract)","provider":"PubTator (NCBI)"},{"exact":"These associations include ERAP1, CCR1-CCR3, STAT4, KLRC4, GIMAP4, and TNFAIP3 in Behçet's disease; BLK and CD40 in Kawasaki disease; SERPINA1 and SEMA6A in antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibody associated vasculitides; IL12B and FCGR2A/ FCGR2A in Takayasu arteritis; and CECR1 in a newly defined vascular inflammatory syndrome associated with adenosine deaminase (ADA2) deficiency.","tags":[{"name":"TNFAIP3","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000118503"},{"name":"Kawasaki disease","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0004246"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/MED/25405820#opentargets-4c719f1a54efcabb4c9820eb426205aa","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Abstract (http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"These associations include ERAP1, CCR1-CCR3, STAT4, KLRC4, GIMAP4, and TNFAIP3 in Behçet's disease; BLK and CD40 in Kawasaki disease; SERPINA1 and SEMA6A in antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibody associated vasculitides; IL12B and FCGR2A/ FCGR2A in Takayasu arteritis; and CECR1 in a newly defined vascular inflammatory syndrome associated with adenosine deaminase (ADA2) deficiency.","tags":[{"name":"ERAP1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000164307"},{"name":"Behçet's disease","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0003780"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/MED/25405820#opentargets-e3fe39feb216104fbc33e42ff253cb80","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Abstract (http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"<h4>Purpose of review</h4>We aim to give an overview of the recent progress in the knowledge of the genetic component of vasculitides.<h4>Recent findings</h4>Using a state-of-the-art imputation method to analyse the major histocompatibility complex (MHC) region, Ombrello and colleagues narrowed down the association between human leukocyte antigen (HLA)-B51 and Behçet's disease to a model of five amino acids of the HLA-B molecule involved in the binding of the antigen, the interactions with receptors on CD8 T cells and natural killer cells, and the signal peptide of HLA-B, suggesting a crucial role of the cellular cytotoxicity on this disease.","tags":[{"name":"MHC","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000204525"},{"name":"Behçet's disease","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0003780"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/MED/25405820#opentargets-d9dec8e4622e1d8d3b12589a70ca21aa","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Abstract (http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"These associations include ERAP1, CCR1-CCR3, STAT4, KLRC4, GIMAP4, and TNFAIP3 in Behçet's disease; BLK and CD40 in Kawasaki disease; SERPINA1 and SEMA6A in antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibody associated vasculitides; IL12B and FCGR2A/ FCGR2A in Takayasu arteritis; and CECR1 in a newly defined vascular inflammatory syndrome associated with adenosine deaminase (ADA2) deficiency.","tags":[{"name":"CCR1","uri":"https://www.ensembl.org/Homo_sapiens/Gene/Summary?db=core;g=ENSG00000163823"},{"name":"Kawasaki disease","uri":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/efo/terms?short_form=EFO_0004246"}],"id":"http://europepmc.org/article/MED/25405820#opentargets-038b6101ad2baec3cf96629604086d23","type":"Gene Disease Relationship","section":"Abstract (http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract)","provider":"Open Targets Platform"},{"exact":"These